adjudication.rationale:
Yes. In `packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/parseRefreshTokenResponse.ts`, after parsing the token refresh response, the code does:

```ts
if (!refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token) {
  refreshTokenResponse.data.refresh_token = "refresh_token";
}
```

When `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` and `CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT` are set, it uses `minimumTokenResponseSchema`, which does not require/ensure `refresh_token`, so this branch can run and inject the literal string. Call sites like Office365 then merge/store the parsed data into credentials (`o365AuthCredentials = { ...o365AuthCredentials, ...(tokenResponse.success && tokenResponse.data) }`), which can overwrite the real stored refresh token with the literal placeholder. This is a concrete correctness defect introduced by the diff.
